'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... isp_hub75_morph7seg.spin2
''   Purpose.... One morphing digit: its stroke figure, and the drawing of every part that changed
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2021 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Jan 2021
''   Updated.... 13 Oct 2026
''   Version.... v1.0.0
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ The figure (spec R-4.3). A digit is the 2021 figure drawn with a round pen of thickness T: straight
  runs on its centre lines, a quarter-circle joint at every corner, round free ends, anti-aliased. The
  seven segments are how it moves, never how it looks: nothing drawn reads as a 7-segment display.

  Geometry, in digit-local pixels (u right, v down, from the digit's top-left). With segment length L,
  P = L + 1 (the 2021 spacing of the centre lines), q = (T + 1) / 2 rounded down and e = 1 when T is
  even (isp_hub75_morphMask.capsulePhase()):
      digit width  W = P + T,   digit height  H = 2P + T        (T = 1: the 2021 digit, L + 2 by 2L + 3)
  Each part draws through one of the group's masks (isp_hub75_morphMask), placed at (u0, v0):

      straight runs (straight mask)      A  (q, 0)   G  (q, P)   D  (q, 2P)       horizontal
                                         F  (0, q)   E  (0, P + q)                vertical (transposed)
                                         B  (P, q)   C  (P, P + q)
      corners (arc mask)                 A-F (0, 0)        A-B (P - 1, 0) mirrored across
                                         D-E (0, 2P - 1)   D-C (P - 1, 2P - 1) mirrored down / both
      side joins (join mask, vertical)   F-E (0, P - q - e)      B-C (P, P - q - e)
      the middle meeting a side (arc)    F-G (0, P - 1)    E-G (0, P)    B-G (P - 1, P - 1)    C-G (P - 1, P)

  A segment lights its straight run. A joint lights where both its segments do: at the lower of their
  lit shares at its end (jointLevel()), so it lights as the second segment's growth reaches it and goes
  dark as soon as either leaves it. Where a side's two segments are both lit the side is one continuous
  stroke; where the middle meets one of them it bends into it; where it meets both it is a T.

  Drawing (spec R-9.3). Each frame the digit asks every segment for its state, works out the local
  rectangle each changed part touched, and redraws only those rectangles. A rectangle is drawn in bands
  that fit levelBuffer, in two passes of inline PASM: composeBand() keeps, for every pixel, the brightest
  level any part gives it (a part's mask byte times its lit share or level): pieces overlap where they
  meet, and the brighter one wins, so the union is one stroke with no seam. drawBand() then carries the
  band onto the display through the group's turn, clipped, by cells (panels), each pixel's level looked
  up in the group's intensity ramp (isp_hub75_morphColor).
}

CON ' public control values

    DIGIT_NO_VALUE = -2   ' digit value when NOT [0-9]
    DIGIT_HIDDEN = -1     ' digit value when NOT [0-9]

    WITH_WRAP = TRUE
    WITHOUT_WRAP = FALSE
    MAX_SEGMENTS = 7
    LAST_SEGMENT = MAX_SEGMENTS - 1     ' index of the last segment slot (segments[] runs from 0)
    ' the joints, each lit where both of its segments are (see the geometry above), then the colon
    #MAX_SEGMENTS, SLOT_CORNER_AF, SLOT_CORNER_AB, SLOT_CORNER_DE, SLOT_CORNER_DC, SLOT_JOIN_FE, SLOT_BEND_FG, SLOT_BEND_EG, SLOT_JOIN_BC, SLOT_BEND_BG, SLOT_BEND_CG
    MAX_JOINTS = SLOT_BEND_CG - LAST_SEGMENT
    SLOT_COLON_UPPER = SLOT_BEND_CG + 1 ' a clock digit also draws the colon after it: two round dots (setColon())
    SLOT_COLON_LOWER = SLOT_COLON_UPPER + 1
    MAX_SLOTS = SLOT_COLON_LOWER + 1    ' every slot composeBand() composites
    LAST_SLOT = MAX_SLOTS - 1

CON ' drawing

    LEVEL_FULL = 255                    ' a fully lit pixel (mask byte, lit share and ramp index)
    LEVEL_ROUND = LEVEL_FULL / 2        ' added before dividing by LEVEL_FULL, to round to nearest
    ' a drawing context (CTX_LONGS longs, owned by the group; see setContext()): where its pixels land,
    '   screen x = CTX_XX * gx + CTX_XY * gy + CTX_X0,  screen y = CTX_YX * gx + CTX_YY * gy + CTX_Y0
    ' for (gx, gy) in group coordinates (each coefficient -1, 0 or 1: a quarter-turn rotation), and the
    ' rectangle of the display its digits may draw in (inclusive)
    #0, CTX_XX, CTX_XY, CTX_X0, CTX_YX, CTX_YY, CTX_Y0, CTX_CLIP_LEFT, CTX_CLIP_TOP, CTX_CLIP_RIGHT, CTX_CLIP_BOTTOM
    CTX_LONGS = CTX_CLIP_BOTTOM + 1

    ' one slot's entry in slotTable (longs): what composeBand() reads for it. A part's mask byte for local
    ' pixel (u, v) is at F_MASK + u * F_STEP_U + v * F_STEP_V (the steps transpose or mirror the mask), and a
    ' snake's lit share at F_LIT + u * F_LIT_U + v * F_LIT_V. F_PARAM is a level (MODE_LEVEL), or a slide's
    ' offset (MODE_SLIDE: the column F_SLIDE_U0 .. + F_SLIDE_WIDTH - 1 moved sideways). All but F_MODE, F_PARAM and
    ' a segment's box are fixed for a figure (setFigure()).
    #0, F_MODE, F_BOX_U0, F_BOX_V0, F_BOX_U1, F_BOX_V1, F_MASK, F_STEP_U, F_STEP_V, F_PARAM, F_LIT, F_LIT_U, F_LIT_V, F_SLIDE_U0, F_SLIDE_WIDTH
    SLOT_LONGS = F_SLIDE_WIDTH + 1
    SLOT_TABLE_LONGS = SLOT_LONGS * MAX_SLOTS
    #0, BOX_U0, BOX_V0, BOX_U1, BOX_V1  ' a home box in homeBoxes (longs)
    BOX_LONGS = BOX_V1 + 1
    MAX_SEGMENT_LENGTH = 128            ' the longest segment a digit can draw
    LIT_COLUMNS = MAX_SEGMENT_LENGTH + 1    ' a straight mask's columns at most (the length, plus one for an even stroke)
    LEVEL_BUFFER_BYTES = 2048           ' one band's levels: a rectangle is drawn in bands of whole rows that fit
    MAX_DIRTY = 8                       ' the rectangles one frame of a digit redraws, after merging ...
    MERGE_SLACK_PIXELS = 256            ' ... two merge when their union is at most this many pixels more than the two:
                                        '   about what one more rectangle's fixed cost (calls, cells, clipping) is worth
    #0, DIRTY_U0, DIRTY_V0, DIRTY_U1, DIRTY_V1, DIRTY_AREA     ' a noted rectangle (inclusive) and its pixels
    DIRTY_LONGS = DIRTY_AREA + 1
    SUBPIXEL_SHIFT = 8                  ' positions are in 1/256 pixel (morphSegment.SUBPIXELS)
    SUBPIXEL_MASK = segments.SUBPIXELS - 1
    SHARE_SHIFT = 12                    ' lit-share arithmetic is Q12
    SHARE_ONE = 1 << SHARE_SHIFT
    SHARE_HALF = SHARE_ONE / 2
    SQUARE_HALF_SHIFT = SHARE_SHIFT + 1 ' u^2 / 2 in Q12: (u * u) >> 13
    NEXT_ONE = 1                        ' one pixel, column or row further on
    MIRRORED = -1                       ' a mask step that runs backwards: the arc mirrored
    BYTES_PER_LONG = 4
    LONG_SHIFT = 2                      ' a long index times BYTES_PER_LONG
    BYTE_BITS = 8                       ' the next byte of a packed color
    MAX_DIGIT_VALUE = 9
    #0, END_START, END_FAR              ' a segment's end at a joint: its first mask column, or its last ...
    SHARES_PER_SEGMENT = 2              ' ... each segment's two ends' lit shares in frameShares

OBJ

    segments[MAX_SEGMENTS]     : "isp_hub75_morphSegment"
    hub75Bffrs                 : "isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess"    ' the address rule (mountedBlockRun) and the window watch
    figure                     : "isp_hub75_morphMask"         ' where each mask lies in the group's buffer (no state)

DAT ' shared drawing tables: one cog draws, one digit at a time, so one copy serves every digit

    slotTable       long    0[SLOT_TABLE_LONGS]                 ' this frame's state of every slot, for composeBand() (F_ fields)
    homeBoxes       long    0[MAX_SLOTS * BOX_LONGS]            ' each part's box at rest (local, inclusive)
    litTable        byte    0[MAX_SEGMENTS * LIT_COLUMNS]       ' this frame's snake lit shares, per segment slot and mask column
    levelBuffer     byte    0[LEVEL_BUFFER_BYTES]               ' one band's composited levels, row-major
    dirtyRects      long    0[MAX_DIRTY * DIRTY_LONGS]          ' this frame's rectangles to redraw (local, inclusive) ...
    dirtyCount      long    0                                   ' ... and how many
    ' the figure the tables above hold (setFigure()): the digits of one group share it, so it is set again
    ' only when a digit of another figure draws
    figureMasks     long    0
    figureLength    long    0
    figureStroke    long    0

    ' which segment slots are vertical (G, F, E, D, C, B, A)
    slotVertical    byte    FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
    ' each joint's two segment ends, as frameShares indexes: slot x SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + end (SLOT_CORNER_AF .. SLOT_BEND_CG)
    jointShareA     byte    6 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 6 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR, 2 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR
                    byte    4 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR, 1 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR, 1 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR
                    byte    2 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 5 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR, 5 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR
                    byte    4 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START
    jointShareB     byte    1 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 5 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 3 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START
                    byte    3 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR, 2 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 0 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START
                    byte    0 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 4 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START, 0 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR
                    byte    0 * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR

VAR ' per digit
    long    chainIndex
    long    currValue
    long    digitGY             ' the digit's top-left in its group's coordinates (the display's, with no group)
    long    digitGX
    long    digitWidth
    long    digitHeight
    long    segLength           ' the segment length L, and the stroke T
    long    stroke
    long    segCols             ' the straight mask's columns: a segment's length along itself
    long    pMasks              ' the group's masks: isp_hub75_morphMask.buildFigure()
    long    pRamp               ' the group's intensity ramp: 256 packed colors
    long    bNeedsRender        ' TRUE from a command until the moves it started have been drawn to their end
    long    bColon              ' TRUE when this digit draws a colon after it (setColon())
    long    colonLeftU          ' the colon's dots: left column, side, and the two dots' top rows (digit-local)
    long    colonDotSize
    long    colonUpperV
    long    colonLowerV
    long    colonLevel          ' the dots' level now (0-255, through the ramp), and the level drawn last
    long    drawnColonLevel
    long    cellRows            ' one cell's (panel's) size as mounted: blocks never cross a cell
    long    cellColumns

    ' the state drawn last, per segment slot (renderState() values)
    long    drawnMode[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    long    drawnHead[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    long    drawnTail[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    long    drawnFromEnd[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    long    drawnOn[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    long    drawnOffset[MAX_SEGMENTS]
    byte    drawnJoint[MAX_JOINTS]   ' each joint's level drawn last
    long    pCtx                ' the drawing context in use: the group's (setContext()), or ownCtx
    long    screenOriginX       ' where digit pixel (0, 0) lands on the display, and the context's coefficients
    long    screenOriginY       '   and clip rectangle, copied at placement (placeDigit()) so drawing reads none
    long    coefXX              '   of them through pCtx
    long    coefXY
    long    coefYX
    long    coefYY
    long    clipLeft
    long    clipTop
    long    clipRight
    long    clipBottom
    long    ownCtx[CTX_LONGS]   ' a digit with no group draws unrotated, clipped to the display

PUB null()
'' This is NOT a top level object
''

PUB initialize(nChainIndex, nPhysicalRows, nPhysicalColumns) | segmentIndex
'' Set the display this digit draws on, and turn every segment off.
''
'' @param nChainIndex - the index of the adapter (chain of panels) this digit draws on
'' @param nPhysicalRows - the display's rows, as mounted
'' @param nPhysicalColumns - the display's columns, as mounted

    chainIndex := nChainIndex
    cellRows, cellColumns := hub75Bffrs.cellSizeInPixels(nChainIndex)
    longfill(@ownCtx, 0, CTX_LONGS)                             ' screen = group coordinates:
    ownCtx[CTX_XX] := ownCtx[CTX_YY] := NEXT_ONE                '   x = gx, y = gy
    ownCtx[CTX_CLIP_RIGHT] := nPhysicalColumns - NEXT_ONE
    ownCtx[CTX_CLIP_BOTTOM] := nPhysicalRows - NEXT_ONE
    pCtx := @ownCtx
    currValue := DIGIT_NO_VALUE
    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        segments[segmentIndex].initialize()
        drawnMode[segmentIndex] := segments.MODE_NONE

PUB digitSize(segmentLength, thickness) : width, height
'' The pixel size of a digit with this segment length and stroke (see the geometry above).
''
'' @param segmentLength - the segment length L, in pixels
'' @param thickness - the stroke T, in pixels
'' @returns width - W = L + 1 + T
'' @returns height - H = 2(L + 1) + T

    width := segmentLength + NEXT_ONE + thickness
    height := (segmentLength + NEXT_ONE) << NEXT_ONE + thickness

PUB placeDigit(row, column, segmentLength, thickness, digitValue, pFigureMasks, pColorRamp, tailX256) : width, height | segmentIndex
'' Place this digit with its top-left at (row, column) and show digitValue (DIGIT_HIDDEN shows nothing).
'' The group has built the figure's masks (isp_hub75_morphMask.buildFigure()) and the ramp; the digit is
'' drawn by the next animate().
''
'' @param row - the digit's top row on the display
'' @param column - the digit's left column on the display
'' @param segmentLength - the segment length L, in pixels
'' @param thickness - the stroke T, in pixels
'' @param digitValue - 0-9, or DIGIT_HIDDEN
'' @param pFigureMasks - the group's masks
'' @param pColorRamp - the group's intensity ramp
'' @param tailX256 - the snake tail, in 1/256 pixel
'' @returns width - the digit's width in pixels
'' @returns height - the digit's height in pixels

' Local Variables:
' @local segmentIndex - the slot being placed

    digitGX := column
    digitGY := row
    coefXX := LONG[pCtx][CTX_XX]                                ' the group's transform, copied once
    coefXY := LONG[pCtx][CTX_XY]
    coefYX := LONG[pCtx][CTX_YX]
    coefYY := LONG[pCtx][CTX_YY]
    screenOriginX := coefXX * digitGX + coefXY * digitGY + LONG[pCtx][CTX_X0]
    screenOriginY := coefYX * digitGX + coefYY * digitGY + LONG[pCtx][CTX_Y0]
    clipLeft := LONG[pCtx][CTX_CLIP_LEFT]
    clipTop := LONG[pCtx][CTX_CLIP_TOP]
    clipRight := LONG[pCtx][CTX_CLIP_RIGHT]
    clipBottom := LONG[pCtx][CTX_CLIP_BOTTOM]
    segLength := segmentLength
    stroke := thickness
    segCols := figure.straightColumns(thickness, segmentLength)
    pMasks := pFigureMasks
    pRamp := pColorRamp
    width, height := digitSize(segmentLength, thickness)
    digitWidth := width
    digitHeight := height
    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        segments[segmentIndex].placeSegment(NEXT_ONE << segmentIndex, segCols << SUBPIXEL_SHIFT, (segmentLength + NEXT_ONE) << SUBPIXEL_SHIFT, tailX256)
        drawnMode[segmentIndex] := segments.MODE_NONE
    bytefill(@drawnJoint, 0, MAX_JOINTS)
    currValue := DIGIT_NO_VALUE
    bNeedsRender := FALSE
    bColon := FALSE
    colonLevel := drawnColonLevel := 0
    if digitValue <> DIGIT_HIDDEN
        reconfigureForDigit(digitValue)

PUB setValue(digitValue)
'' Show digitValue: 0-9 morphs from the value shown, DIGIT_HIDDEN shows nothing.
''
'' @param digitValue - 0-9, or DIGIT_HIDDEN

    if currValue <> digitValue
        reconfigureForDigit(digitValue)

PUB incrementValue(shouldWrap) | nextValue
'' Show the next digit (0 -> 9); after 9, wrap to 0 when shouldWrap is WITH_WRAP, else stay at 9.
''
'' @param shouldWrap - WITH_WRAP or WITHOUT_WRAP

    nextValue := currValue + NEXT_ONE
    if nextValue > MAX_DIGIT_VALUE
        if shouldWrap <> WITH_WRAP
            nextValue := MAX_DIGIT_VALUE
        else
            nextValue := 0
    setValue(nextValue)

PUB isAnimationComplete() : bComplete | segmentIndex
'' Return TRUE when no segment of this digit is moving.
''
'' @returns bComplete - TRUE when every segment is at rest

    bComplete := TRUE
    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        if not segments[segmentIndex].isMovementComplete()
            bComplete := FALSE
            quit

PUB animate(nowMs) : movingCount | segmentIndex
'' Move every segment to its position for time nowMs, then redraw what changed (a digit at rest draws nothing).
''
'' @param nowMs - The frame's time in ms, from isp_hub75_morphTime.update(): the same value for every group, digit and segment of a frame
'' @returns movingCount - Number of this digit's segments still moving after this call; 0 when the digit is at rest

' Local Variables:
' @local segmentIndex - Index of the segment being moved

    movingCount := 0
    if bNeedsRender                                     ' early-out: an idle digit costs one test (R-9.3)
        repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
            movingCount += segments[segmentIndex].animate(nowMs)
        drawChanges()
        bNeedsRender := movingCount > 0                 ' stays TRUE while a move is in flight

PUB setMotion(durationMs, easeStyle) | segmentIndex
'' Set how every segment of this digit moves: the duration of each move and its easing.
''
'' @param durationMs - Duration of each move in ms; morphCounters.setMoveDuration() checks the range
'' @param easeStyle - Easing style, timeBase.EASE_LINEAR or timeBase.EASE_SMOOTH; morphCounters.setEasing() checks it

' Local Variables:
' @local segmentIndex - Index of the segment being set

    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        segments[segmentIndex].setMotion(durationMs, easeStyle)

PUB setTail(tailX256) | segmentIndex
'' Set every segment's snake tail.
''
'' @param tailX256 - the snake tail, in 1/256 pixel

' Local Variables:
' @local segmentIndex - Index of the segment being set

    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        segments[segmentIndex].setTail(tailX256)

PUB commandSegment(segmentIndex, commandBits) : status
'' Send one command byte to one segment (for tests; the digit's own transitions come from the table).
''
'' @param segmentIndex - the slot, 0 (G) to LAST_SEGMENT (A)
'' @param commandBits - Command byte %GGG_AAAT
'' @returns status - the segment's status: morphStatus SUCCESS or E_BAD_COMMAND

    status := segments[segmentIndex].commandSegment(commandBits)
    bNeedsRender := TRUE

PUB morphOut() | segmentIndex
'' Turn every lit segment off with a snake (horizontals left to right, verticals top down): the digit morphs out
'' and ends hidden.
''

    repeat segmentIndex from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        if slotVertical[segmentIndex]
            segments[segmentIndex].commandSegment(segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN)
        else
            segments[segmentIndex].commandSegment(segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    currValue := DIGIT_HIDDEN
    bNeedsRender := TRUE

PUB value() : digitValue
'' The digit this digit shows, or is morphing to: 0-9, DIGIT_HIDDEN, or DIGIT_NO_VALUE before its first value.
''
'' @returns digitValue - the digit's value

    digitValue := currValue

PUB setColon(leftU, dotSide, upperV, lowerV)
'' Draw a colon after this digit: two round dots (digit-local), lit fully until setColonLevel() changes it. The
'' group's masks hold a dot of this side (isp_hub75_morphMask.buildFigure()).
''
'' @param leftU - the dots' left column, digit-local (past the digit's right edge)
'' @param dotSide - each dot's side, in pixels
'' @param upperV - the upper dot's top row, digit-local
'' @param lowerV - the lower dot's top row, digit-local

    bColon := TRUE
    colonLeftU := leftU
    colonDotSize := dotSide
    colonUpperV := upperV
    colonLowerV := lowerV
    colonLevel := LEVEL_FULL
    drawnColonLevel := 0
    bNeedsRender := TRUE

PUB setColonLevel(level)
'' Light the colon at a level: 0 (dark) to LEVEL_FULL (the group's color), through the group's ramp.
''
'' @param level - 0 to LEVEL_FULL

    if bColon and level <> colonLevel
        colonLevel := level
        bNeedsRender := TRUE

PUB setContext(pGroupContext)
'' Draw through a group's context: its transform and its clip rectangle (CTX_ fields), taken at the next
'' placeDigit(). The group owns the block and fills it before placing its digits.
''
'' @param pGroupContext - hub address of the group's CTX_LONGS longs

    pCtx := pGroupContext

PRI setFigure() | period, inset, joinTop, pStraight, pJoin
' Fill the shared tables' fixed parts for this digit's figure: every part's home box, and where its mask lies
' and how it is read (see the geometry above). Skipped when they already hold this figure.

' Local Variables:
' @local period - P = L + 1: the spacing of the centre lines
' @local inset - q = (T + 1) / 2: where a straight run's mask starts past its corner
' @local joinTop - a side join's top row: P - q - e
' @local pStraight, pJoin - the straight and join masks

    if figureMasks <> pMasks or figureLength <> segLength or figureStroke <> stroke
        figureMasks, figureLength, figureStroke := pMasks, segLength, stroke
        period := segLength + NEXT_ONE
        inset := (stroke + NEXT_ONE) >> NEXT_ONE
        joinTop := period - inset - figure.capsulePhase(stroke)
        pStraight := pMasks
        pJoin := pMasks + figure.joinOffset(stroke, segLength)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_TOP_A, inset, 0, FALSE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_MIDDLE_G, inset, period, FALSE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_BOTTOM_D, inset, period << NEXT_ONE, FALSE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_LEFT_F, 0, inset, TRUE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_LEFT_E, 0, period + inset, TRUE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_RIGHT_B, period, inset, TRUE, pStraight, segCols)
        setSlotMask(encod segments.SOR_RIGHT_C, period, period + inset, TRUE, pStraight, segCols)
        setJoinSlot(SLOT_JOIN_FE, 0, joinTop, pJoin)
        setJoinSlot(SLOT_JOIN_BC, period, joinTop, pJoin)
        setArc(SLOT_CORNER_AF, 0, 0, NEXT_ONE, NEXT_ONE)
        setArc(SLOT_CORNER_AB, period - NEXT_ONE, 0, MIRRORED, NEXT_ONE)
        setArc(SLOT_CORNER_DE, 0, period << NEXT_ONE - NEXT_ONE, NEXT_ONE, MIRRORED)
        setArc(SLOT_CORNER_DC, period - NEXT_ONE, period << NEXT_ONE - NEXT_ONE, MIRRORED, MIRRORED)
        setArc(SLOT_BEND_FG, 0, period - NEXT_ONE, NEXT_ONE, MIRRORED)
        setArc(SLOT_BEND_EG, 0, period, NEXT_ONE, NEXT_ONE)
        setArc(SLOT_BEND_BG, period - NEXT_ONE, period - NEXT_ONE, MIRRORED, MIRRORED)
        setArc(SLOT_BEND_CG, period - NEXT_ONE, period, MIRRORED, NEXT_ONE)

PRI setJoinSlot(slot, leftU, topV, pMask)
' A side join: the join mask at (leftU, topV), along v.

    setSlotMask(slot, leftU, topV, TRUE, pMask, figure.joinColumns(stroke))

PRI setSlotMask(slot, leftU, topV, bVertical, pMask, nCols) | pBox, pEntry
' A capsule's fixed fields: its home box, its mask read as it is (along u) or transposed (along v), and its
' lit shares along it; a vertical one slides sideways over its stroke's columns.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBox - the slot's home box
' @local pEntry - the slot's slotTable entry

    pBox := @homeBoxes + slot * BOX_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    pEntry := @slotTable + slot * SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    LONG[pBox][BOX_U0], LONG[pBox][BOX_V0] := leftU, topV
    LONG[pEntry][F_SLIDE_U0] := leftU
    LONG[pEntry][F_SLIDE_WIDTH] := stroke
    if bVertical
        LONG[pBox][BOX_U1], LONG[pBox][BOX_V1] := leftU + stroke - NEXT_ONE, topV + nCols - NEXT_ONE
        LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_U], LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V] := nCols, NEXT_ONE
        LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_U], LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_V] := 0, NEXT_ONE
    else
        LONG[pBox][BOX_U1], LONG[pBox][BOX_V1] := leftU + nCols - NEXT_ONE, topV + stroke - NEXT_ONE
        LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_U], LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V] := NEXT_ONE, nCols
        LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_U], LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_V] := NEXT_ONE, 0
    LONG[pEntry][F_MASK] := pMask - leftU * LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_U] - topV * LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V]
    LONG[pEntry][F_LIT] := @litTable + slot * LIT_COLUMNS - leftU * LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_U] - topV * LONG[pEntry][F_LIT_V]
    longmove(pEntry + F_BOX_U0 * BYTES_PER_LONG, pBox, BOX_LONGS)

PRI setArc(slot, leftU, topV, stepU, stepV) | side, pBox, pEntry, firstU, firstV
' A corner or bend: the arc mask at (leftU, topV), mirrored across (stepU MIRRORED) and/or down (stepV MIRRORED).

' Local Variables:
' @local side - the arc mask's side
' @local pBox - the slot's home box
' @local pEntry - the slot's slotTable entry
' @local firstU, firstV - the local pixel that reads the mask's first byte

    side := figure.arcSide(stroke)
    pBox := @homeBoxes + slot * BOX_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    pEntry := @slotTable + slot * SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    LONG[pBox][BOX_U0], LONG[pBox][BOX_V0] := leftU, topV
    LONG[pBox][BOX_U1], LONG[pBox][BOX_V1] := leftU + side - NEXT_ONE, topV + side - NEXT_ONE
    firstU := (stepU == MIRRORED) ? LONG[pBox][BOX_U1] : leftU
    firstV := (stepV == MIRRORED) ? LONG[pBox][BOX_V1] : topV
    LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_U] := stepU
    LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V] := stepV * side
    LONG[pEntry][F_MASK] := pMasks + figure.arcOffset(stroke, segLength) - firstU * stepU - firstV * LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V]
    longmove(pEntry + F_BOX_U0 * BYTES_PER_LONG, pBox, BOX_LONGS)

PRI drawChanges() | slot, mode, head, tail, bFromEnd, bOn, offset, colLo, colHi, posLo, posHi, jointIdx, level, pEntry
' Load every part's state for this frame into the shared tables and note the local rectangle each changed part
' touched (old and new); then redraw the noted rectangles, each compositing every part's state this frame.

' Local Variables:
' @local slot - the segment slot
' @local mode, head, tail, bFromEnd, bOn, offset - the slot's renderState() this frame
' @local colLo, colHi - a snake's changed columns, from its start end
' @local posLo, posHi - the lower and higher of two positions, in 1/256 pixel
' @local jointIdx - the joint being loaded
' @local level - a segment's lit share at both ends when at rest; a joint's level
' @local pEntry - the slot's slotTable entry

    setFigure()
    pEntry := @slotTable
    repeat slot from 0 to LAST_SEGMENT
        mode, head, tail, bFromEnd, bOn, offset := segments[slot].renderState()
        LONG[pEntry][F_MODE] := mode
        LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U1], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V1] := stateBox(slot, mode, offset)
        LONG[pEntry][F_PARAM] := offset
        if mode == segments.MODE_SNAKE                                      ' its lit shares, and at its two ends (a sliding
            fillLitShares(slot, head, tail, bOn, bFromEnd)                  '   column is away from its joints)
            frameShares[slot * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START] := litTable[slot * LIT_COLUMNS]
            frameShares[slot * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR] := litTable[slot * LIT_COLUMNS + segCols - NEXT_ONE]
        else
            level := (mode == segments.MODE_FULL) ? LEVEL_FULL : 0
            frameShares[slot * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_START] := frameShares[slot * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT + END_FAR] := level
        if mode <> drawnMode[slot] or tail <> drawnTail[slot] or bFromEnd <> drawnFromEnd[slot] or bOn <> drawnOn[slot]
            drawStateRect(slot, drawnMode[slot], drawnOffset[slot])         ' where it was ...
            drawStateRect(slot, mode, offset)                               ' ... and where it is
        elseif mode == segments.MODE_SNAKE and head <> drawnHead[slot]
            posLo := (head <# drawnHead[slot]) - tail - segments.SUBPIXELS
            posHi := (head #> drawnHead[slot]) + segments.SUBPIXELS
            colLo := (posLo sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT) #> 0
            colHi := (posHi sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT) <# (segCols - NEXT_ONE)
            if bFromEnd                                                     ' columns counted from the far end: mirror the range
                posLo := segCols - NEXT_ONE - colHi
                colHi := segCols - NEXT_ONE - colLo
                colLo := posLo
            if colLo <= colHi
                drawAlong(slot, colLo, colHi)
        elseif mode == segments.MODE_SLIDE and offset <> drawnOffset[slot]
            drawSlideRect(slot, drawnOffset[slot], offset)
        drawnMode[slot] := mode
        drawnHead[slot] := head
        drawnTail[slot] := tail
        drawnFromEnd[slot] := bFromEnd
        drawnOn[slot] := bOn
        drawnOffset[slot] := offset
        pEntry += SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    repeat jointIdx from 0 to MAX_JOINTS - NEXT_ONE                         ' a joint: the lower of its two ends' lit shares
        level := frameShares[jointShareA[jointIdx]] <# frameShares[jointShareB[jointIdx]]
        LONG[pEntry][F_MODE] := (level > 0) ? segments.MODE_LEVEL : segments.MODE_NONE
        LONG[pEntry][F_PARAM] := level
        if level <> drawnJoint[jointIdx]
            drawLocalRect(LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U1], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V1])
            drawnJoint[jointIdx] := level
        pEntry += SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    colonStateLoad(SLOT_COLON_UPPER, colonUpperV)
    colonStateLoad(SLOT_COLON_LOWER, colonLowerV)
    if bColon and colonLevel <> drawnColonLevel                         ' the colon's level changed: redraw its dots
        drawLocalRect(colonBox(colonUpperV))
        drawLocalRect(colonBox(colonLowerV))
        drawnColonLevel := colonLevel
    flushDirty()

DAT ' this frame's lit shares at each segment's ends, for its joints (the digits draw one at a time, so one copy serves all)

    frameShares     byte    0[MAX_SEGMENTS * SHARES_PER_SEGMENT]    ' each segment's lit share at its start end and its far end

PRI colonStateLoad(slot, topV) | pEntry
' Load one colon dot's slotTable entry: the dot mask at the colon's level, or nothing (no colon, or level 0).

' Local Variables:
' @local pEntry - the slot's slotTable entry

    pEntry := @slotTable + slot * SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    if bColon and colonLevel > 0
        LONG[pEntry][F_MODE] := segments.MODE_LEVEL
        LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V0], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_U1], LONG[pEntry][F_BOX_V1] := colonBox(topV)
        LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_U], LONG[pEntry][F_STEP_V] := NEXT_ONE, colonDotSize
        LONG[pEntry][F_MASK] := pMasks + figure.dotOffset(stroke, segLength) - colonLeftU - topV * colonDotSize
        LONG[pEntry][F_PARAM] := colonLevel
    else
        LONG[pEntry][F_MODE] := segments.MODE_NONE              ' the shared table may hold the last colon digit's dot

PRI colonBox(topV) : leftU, boxTopV, rightU, bottomV
' One colon dot's box, digit-local: the dot whose top row is topV.

    leftU, boxTopV := colonLeftU, topV
    rightU, bottomV := colonLeftU + colonDotSize - NEXT_ONE, topV + colonDotSize - NEXT_ONE

PRI stateBox(slot, mode, offset) : leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV | pBox
' A slot's box (local, inclusive) in this mode: a slide's column moved sideways by offset (1/256 pixel), any
' other mode at home.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBox - the slot's home box

    pBox := @homeBoxes + slot * BOX_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV := LONG[pBox][BOX_U0], LONG[pBox][BOX_V0], LONG[pBox][BOX_U1], LONG[pBox][BOX_V1]
    if mode == segments.MODE_SLIDE
        leftU += offset sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
        rightU += (offset + SUBPIXEL_MASK) sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT

PRI drawStateRect(slot, mode, offset) | leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV
' Redraw the box a slot covers in this mode at this offset (nothing for MODE_NONE).

    if mode <> segments.MODE_NONE
        leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV := stateBox(slot, mode, offset)
        drawLocalRect(leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV)

PRI drawSlideRect(slot, fromOffset, toOffset) | leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV, otherLeftU, otherRightU
' Redraw where a sliding column was and where it is now, as one rectangle: the two boxes overlap.

    leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV := stateBox(slot, segments.MODE_SLIDE, fromOffset)
    otherLeftU, _, otherRightU, _ := stateBox(slot, segments.MODE_SLIDE, toOffset)
    drawLocalRect(leftU <# otherLeftU, topV, rightU #> otherRightU, bottomV)

PRI drawAlong(slot, colLo, colHi) | pBox
' Redraw columns colLo..colHi of a segment's straight run (along it), its full width.

' Local Variables:
' @local pBox - the slot's home box

    pBox := @homeBoxes + slot * BOX_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    if slotVertical[slot]
        drawLocalRect(LONG[pBox][BOX_U0], LONG[pBox][BOX_V0] + colLo, LONG[pBox][BOX_U1], LONG[pBox][BOX_V0] + colHi)
    else
        drawLocalRect(LONG[pBox][BOX_U0] + colLo, LONG[pBox][BOX_V0], LONG[pBox][BOX_U0] + colHi, LONG[pBox][BOX_V1])

PRI drawLocalRect(leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV) | idx, pRect, unionU0, unionV0, unionU1, unionV1, area
' Note a local rectangle to redraw this frame (flushDirty() draws them): merged into one already noted when
' their union costs less than drawing both (MERGE_SLACK_PIXELS), and the result merged again the same way.

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - the noted rectangle being compared
' @local pRect - its entry
' @local unionU0, unionV0, unionU1, unionV1 - the union of the two
' @local area - this rectangle's pixels

    area := (rightU - leftU + NEXT_ONE) * (bottomV - topV + NEXT_ONE)
    idx := 0
    pRect := @dirtyRects
    repeat while idx < dirtyCount
        unionU0 := leftU <# LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U0]
        unionV0 := topV <# LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V0]
        unionU1 := rightU #> LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U1]
        unionV1 := bottomV #> LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V1]
        if (unionU1 - unionU0 + NEXT_ONE) * (unionV1 - unionV0 + NEXT_ONE) <= area + LONG[pRect][DIRTY_AREA] + MERGE_SLACK_PIXELS or dirtyCount == MAX_DIRTY
            leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV := unionU0, unionV0, unionU1, unionV1      ' take it out, and note the union instead
            area := (rightU - leftU + NEXT_ONE) * (bottomV - topV + NEXT_ONE)
            dirtyCount--
            longmove(pRect, pRect + DIRTY_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG, (dirtyCount - idx) * DIRTY_LONGS)
            idx := 0
            pRect := @dirtyRects
        else
            idx++
            pRect += DIRTY_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
    LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U0], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V0], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U1], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V1], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_AREA] := leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV, area
    dirtyCount++

PRI flushDirty() | idx, pRect
' Redraw every rectangle noted this frame, then forget them.

    repeat idx from 0 to dirtyCount - NEXT_ONE
        pRect := @dirtyRects + idx * DIRTY_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
        drawRect(LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U0], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V0], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_U1], LONG[pRect][DIRTY_V1])
    dirtyCount := 0

PRI drawRect(leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV) | bandWidth, bandRows, bandTop, bandBottom
' Redraw a local rectangle, in bands of whole rows that fit levelBuffer: each band composited (composeBand()),
' then carried onto the display (drawBand()).

' Local Variables:
' @local bandWidth - the rectangle's width: every band's
' @local bandRows - the rows a band holds
' @local bandTop, bandBottom - the band being drawn (inclusive)

    bandWidth := rightU - leftU + NEXT_ONE
    bandRows := LEVEL_BUFFER_BYTES / bandWidth
    bandTop := topV
    repeat while bandTop <= bottomV
        bandBottom := (bandTop + bandRows - NEXT_ONE) <# bottomV
        composeBand(leftU, bandTop, rightU, bandBottom)
        drawBand(leftU, bandTop, rightU, bandBottom)
        bandTop := bandBottom + NEXT_ONE

PRI drawBand(leftU, topV, rightU, bottomV) | firstX, lastX, firstY, lastY, cornerX, cornerY, blockX0, blockX1, blockY0, blockY1, pPixel, rightStep, downStep, blockU, blockV, bandWidth
' Carry a composited band onto the display: through the context's transform, clipped to the context's clip
' rectangle, split into blocks that each lie in one cell (one panel), each block drawn by drawBlock() at the
' address and steps the driver's address rule gives (hub75Bffrs.mountedBlockRun()); then the driver's window
' watch is told what was written.

' Local Variables:
' @local firstX, lastX, firstY, lastY - the band on the display, clipped
' @local cornerX, cornerY - the band's far corner on the display
' @local blockX0, blockX1, blockY0, blockY1 - the block being drawn: the band's part in one cell
' @local pPixel, rightStep, downStep - the block's top-left pixel address and its steps, or NO_PIXEL
' @local blockU, blockV - the block's top-left display pixel in digit coordinates
' @local bandWidth - the band's width: levelBuffer's row length

    bandWidth := rightU - leftU + NEXT_ONE
    firstX, firstY := toScreen(leftU, topV)                     ' a quarter-turn maps a rectangle to a rectangle:
    cornerX, cornerY := toScreen(rightU, bottomV)               ' its two corners bound it
    lastX := (firstX #> cornerX) <# clipRight
    firstX := (firstX <# cornerX) #> clipLeft
    lastY := (firstY #> cornerY) <# clipBottom
    firstY := (firstY <# cornerY) #> clipTop
    if firstX <= lastX and firstY <= lastY
        blockY0 := firstY
        repeat while blockY0 <= lastY
            blockY1 := ((blockY0 / cellRows + NEXT_ONE) * cellRows - NEXT_ONE) <# lastY
            blockX0 := firstX
            repeat while blockX0 <= lastX
                blockX1 := ((blockX0 / cellColumns + NEXT_ONE) * cellColumns - NEXT_ONE) <# lastX
                pPixel, rightStep, downStep := hub75Bffrs.mountedBlockRun(chainIndex, blockY0, blockX0, blockY1 - blockY0 + NEXT_ONE, blockX1 - blockX0 + NEXT_ONE)
                if pPixel <> hub75Bffrs.NO_PIXEL                     ' a cell that holds no panel draws nothing
                    blockU, blockV := toLocal(blockX0, blockY0)
                    ' one pixel right on the display moves (coefXX, coefXY) in (u, v); one down, (coefYX, coefYY)
                    drawBlock(pPixel, rightStep, downStep, (blockV - topV) * bandWidth + blockU - leftU, coefXY * bandWidth + coefXX, coefYY * bandWidth + coefYX, blockX1 - blockX0 + NEXT_ONE, blockY1 - blockY0 + NEXT_ONE)
                blockX0 := blockX1 + NEXT_ONE
            blockY0 := blockY1 + NEXT_ONE
        hub75Bffrs.noteDrawn(chainIndex, firstY, firstX, lastY, lastX)

PRI toScreen(localU, localV) : screenX, screenY
' A digit pixel's place on the display, through the group's transform.

    screenX := screenOriginX + coefXX * localU + coefXY * localV
    screenY := screenOriginY + coefYX * localU + coefYY * localV

PRI toLocal(screenX, screenY) : localU, localV
' A display pixel in digit coordinates: the transform's inverse (a rotation's inverse is its transpose).

    screenX -= screenOriginX
    screenY -= screenOriginY
    localU := coefXX * screenX + coefYX * screenY
    localV := coefXY * screenX + coefYY * screenY

PRI composeBand(bandU0, bandV0, bandU1, bandV1) | pSlots, pBuf, bandWidth, slotsLeft
' Composite one band (local, inclusive) into levelBuffer, inline PASM (cog-exec): every slot's level at every
' pixel of its box inside the band, the brightest kept. A part's level is its mask byte, times its snake's lit
' share or its level (/ 255, rounded), or its mask slid sideways (two columns blended).
'
' @param bandU0, bandV0 - the band's top-left, digit-local
' @param bandU1, bandV1 - its bottom-right, digit-local

' Local Variables (the first 16 longs, mapped to cog registers by name):
' @local pSlots - the slot entry being read
' @local pBuf - levelBuffer
' @local bandWidth - the band's width: levelBuffer's row length
' @local slotsLeft - slots still to composite

    pSlots := @slotTable
    pBuf := @levelBuffer
    bandWidth := bandU1 - bandU0 + NEXT_ONE
    bytefill(pBuf, 0, bandWidth * (bandV1 - bandV0 + NEXT_ONE))
    slotsLeft := MAX_SLOTS
    org
.slot
                setq    #F_BOX_V1                               ' the slot's mode and box first, into rMode ..
                rdlong  rMode, pSlots                           '   (most slots miss the band)
                mov     pRest, pSlots
                add     pSlots, #SLOT_LONGS * BYTES_PER_LONG
                cmp     rMode, #segments.MODE_NONE  wz
    if_z        jmp     #.next
                fges    rBoxU0, bandU0                          ' the slot's box, clipped to the band
                fles    rBoxU1, bandU1
                fges    rBoxV0, bandV0
                fles    rBoxV1, bandV1
                cmps    rBoxU1, rBoxU0          wc
    if_nc       cmps    rBoxV1, rBoxV0          wc
    if_c        jmp     #.next
                add     pRest, #F_MASK * BYTES_PER_LONG         ' then the rest of its entry, into rMask ..
                setq    #SLOT_LONGS - F_MASK - NEXT_ONE
                rdlong  rMask, pRest
                mov     nCols, rBoxU1                           ' the clipped box's size
                sub     nCols, rBoxU0
                add     nCols, #NEXT_ONE
                mov     nRows, rBoxV1
                sub     nRows, rBoxV0
                add     nRows, #NEXT_ONE
                mov     rowMask, rBoxU0                         ' its first pixel's mask byte ...
                muls    rowMask, rStepU
                mov     t1, rBoxV0
                muls    t1, rStepV
                add     rowMask, t1
                add     rowMask, rMask
                mov     rowLit, rBoxU0                          ' ... lit share ...
                muls    rowLit, rLitU
                mov     t1, rBoxV0
                muls    t1, rLitV
                add     rowLit, t1
                add     rowLit, rLit
                mov     rowBuf, rBoxV0                          ' ... and level in the band
                sub     rowBuf, bandV0
                mul     rowBuf, bandWidth                       ' both small: a band holds LEVEL_BUFFER_BYTES
                add     rowBuf, rBoxU0
                sub     rowBuf, bandU0
                add     rowBuf, pBuf
                cmp     rMode, #segments.MODE_SLIDE  wz         ' one loop per mode
    if_z        jmp     #.slide
                cmp     rMode, #segments.MODE_FULL  wz
    if_z        jmp     #.fullRow
                cmp     rMode, #segments.MODE_LEVEL  wz
    if_z        jmp     #.levelRow
.snakeRow                                                       ' snake: the mask byte times the lit share / 255, rounded
                mov     aMask, rowMask
                mov     aLit, rowLit
                mov     aBuf, rowBuf
                mov     colsLeft, nCols
.snakePixel
                rdbyte  level, aMask
                add     aMask, rStepU
                rdbyte  t2, aLit
                add     aLit, rLitU
                mul     level, t2
                add     level, #LEVEL_ROUND + NEXT_ONE
                mov     t2, level
                shr     t2, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                add     level, t2
                shr     level, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                rdbyte  t2, aBuf                                ' the brightest part wins
                fge     t2, level
                wrbyte  t2, aBuf
                add     aBuf, #NEXT_ONE
                djnz    colsLeft, #.snakePixel
                add     rowMask, rStepV
                add     rowLit, rLitV
                add     rowBuf, bandWidth
                djnz    nRows, #.snakeRow
                jmp     #.next

.levelRow                                                       ' level: the mask byte times the level / 255, rounded
                mov     aMask, rowMask
                mov     aBuf, rowBuf
                mov     colsLeft, nCols
.levelPixel
                rdbyte  level, aMask
                add     aMask, rStepU
                mul     level, rParam
                add     level, #LEVEL_ROUND + NEXT_ONE
                mov     t2, level
                shr     t2, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                add     level, t2
                shr     level, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                rdbyte  t2, aBuf
                fge     t2, level
                wrbyte  t2, aBuf
                add     aBuf, #NEXT_ONE
                djnz    colsLeft, #.levelPixel
                add     rowMask, rStepV
                add     rowBuf, bandWidth
                djnz    nRows, #.levelRow
                jmp     #.next

.fullRow                                                        ' full: the mask byte
                mov     aMask, rowMask
                mov     aBuf, rowBuf
                mov     colsLeft, nCols
.fullPixel
                rdbyte  level, aMask
                add     aMask, rStepU
                rdbyte  t2, aBuf
                fge     t2, level
                wrbyte  t2, aBuf
                add     aBuf, #NEXT_ONE
                djnz    colsLeft, #.fullPixel
                add     rowMask, rStepV
                add     rowBuf, bandWidth
                djnz    nRows, #.fullRow
                jmp     #.next

.slide                                                          ' the column moved by rParam (1/256 pixel): pixel u shows
                mov     shift, rParam                           '   the mask at u - k - f, k whole, f the fraction: the
                sar     shift, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT                  '   column u - k weighted 1 - f, the column before it f
                mov     coverNext, rParam
                and     coverNext, #SUBPIXEL_MASK
                mov     t1, shift                               ' the mask byte of column u - k, from column u's
                muls    t1, rStepU
                sub     rowMask, t1
                mov     firstAcross, rBoxU0                     ' column u - k across the run, at the box's left
                sub     firstAcross, shift
                sub     firstAcross, rSlideU0
.slideRow
                mov     aMask, rowMask
                mov     aBuf, rowBuf
                mov     across, firstAcross
                mov     colsLeft, nCols
.slidePixel
                mov     m0, #0
                cmp     across, rSlideWidth     wc              ' unsigned: a column left of the run reads as huge
    if_c        rdbyte  m0, aMask
                mov     m1, #0
                sub     across, #NEXT_ONE
                cmp     across, rSlideWidth     wc
                mov     t1, aMask
                sub     t1, rStepU
    if_c        rdbyte  m1, t1
                add     across, #NEXT_ONE + NEXT_ONE
                mov     t1, ##segments.SUBPIXELS
                sub     t1, coverNext
                mul     m0, t1
                mul     m1, coverNext
                add     m0, m1
                add     m0, #LEVEL_ROUND + NEXT_ONE
                shr     m0, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                rdbyte  t2, aBuf
                fge     t2, m0
                wrbyte  t2, aBuf
                add     aMask, rStepU
                add     aBuf, #NEXT_ONE
                djnz    colsLeft, #.slidePixel
                add     rowMask, rStepV
                add     rowBuf, bandWidth
                djnz    nRows, #.slideRow
.next
                djnz    slotsLeft, #.slot
                ret

rMode           long    0                                       ' the slot's entry (F_ order)
rBoxU0          long    0
rBoxV0          long    0
rBoxU1          long    0
rBoxV1          long    0
rMask           long    0
rStepU          long    0
rStepV          long    0
rParam          long    0
rLit            long    0
rLitU           long    0
rLitV           long    0
rSlideU0        long    0
rSlideWidth     long    0
pRest           long    0                                       ' the rest of the slot's entry
nCols           long    0
nRows           long    0
rowMask         long    0
rowLit          long    0
rowBuf          long    0
aMask           long    0
aLit            long    0
aBuf            long    0
colsLeft        long    0
level           long    0
shift           long    0
coverNext            long    0
firstAcross     long    0
across          long    0
m0              long    0
m1              long    0
t1              long    0
t2              long    0
    end

PRI drawBlock(pPixel, rightStep, downStep, bufIndex, indexStepX, indexStepY, nColumns, nRows) | pBuf, pRampB, rowPixel, colsLeft
' Draw one block in one cell from levelBuffer, inline PASM (cog-exec): each pixel's level through the ramp,
' written as its three bytes (red, green, blue: the driver's writePacked() order).
'
' @param pPixel - hub address of the block's top-left pixel
' @param rightStep - signed bytes to the next pixel right, in this cell
' @param downStep - signed bytes to the next pixel down, in this cell
' @param bufIndex - the block's top-left pixel's index in levelBuffer
' @param indexStepX - the index step for one pixel right on the display
' @param indexStepY - the index step for one pixel down
' @param nColumns - the block's width
' @param nRows - the block's height

' Local Variables (the first 16 longs, mapped to cog registers by name):
' @local pBuf - levelBuffer
' @local pRampB - the group's intensity ramp
' @local rowPixel - the current row's first pixel
' @local colsLeft - pixels left in the current row

    pBuf := @levelBuffer + bufIndex
    pRampB := pRamp
    rowPixel := pPixel
    org
.row
                mov     pix, rowPixel
                mov     pLevel, pBuf
                mov     colsLeft, nColumns
.pixel
                rdbyte  color, pLevel                           ' the level, through the ramp: red, green, blue bytes
                shl     color, #LONG_SHIFT
                add     color, pRampB
                rdlong  color, color
                wrbyte  color, pix
                shr     color, #BYTE_BITS
                mov     t1, pix
                add     t1, #NEXT_ONE
                wrbyte  color, t1
                shr     color, #BYTE_BITS
                add     t1, #NEXT_ONE
                wrbyte  color, t1
                add     pix, rightStep
                add     pLevel, indexStepX
                djnz    colsLeft, #.pixel
                add     rowPixel, downStep
                add     pBuf, indexStepY
                djnz    nRows, #.row
                ret

pix             long    0
pLevel          long    0
color           long    0
t1              long    0
    end

PRI fillLitShares(slot, head, tail, bOn, bFromEnd) | fromStart, distance, pLit, fullBelow, darkFrom, behindLevel, aheadLevel, edgeLeft, lastColumn
' A snake's lit share (0-255) of every mask column, into litTable: the average over the column of
' clamp((head - x) / tail, 0, 1), x measured from the snake's start end (the far end when bFromEnd; head and
' tail in 1/256 pixel); turning on (bOn) lights that, turning off lights the rest.
' Columns wholly behind the moving edge and columns past the head take one level each (bytefill); only the
' columns of the edge itself (about tail + 2) are worked out, in inline PASM (cog-exec, CORDIC divides): with
' G the integral of clamp (0 below 0, x^2 / 2 up to 1, then x - 1/2) and d = head minus the column's near edge,
' the column's average is tail x (G(d / tail) - G((d - 1 px) / tail)), all in Q12.

' Local Variables (the first 16 longs, mapped to cog registers by name):
' @local fromStart - a column's index counted from the snake's start end
' @local distance - head minus the column's near edge, in 1/256 pixel
' @local pLit - this slot's lit shares
' @local fullBelow - columns (from the start end) below this lie wholly behind head - tail
' @local darkFrom - columns (from the start end) from this one on lie at or past the head
' @local behindLevel, aheadLevel - the share behind the edge and past the head
' @local edgeLeft - the edge's columns still to work out
' @local lastColumn - the mask's last column: a column counted from the far end is stored at lastColumn minus it

    pLit := @litTable + slot * LIT_COLUMNS
    fullBelow := (((head - tail) sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT) - NEXT_ONE) #> 0 <# segCols
    darkFrom := ((head + SUBPIXEL_MASK) sar SUBPIXEL_SHIFT) #> fullBelow <# segCols
    behindLevel := bOn ? LEVEL_FULL : 0
    aheadLevel := LEVEL_FULL - behindLevel
    if bFromEnd
        bytefill(pLit + segCols - fullBelow, behindLevel, fullBelow)
        bytefill(pLit, aheadLevel, segCols - darkFrom)
    else
        bytefill(pLit, behindLevel, fullBelow)
        bytefill(pLit + darkFrom, aheadLevel, segCols - darkFrom)
    fromStart := fullBelow
    edgeLeft := darkFrom - fullBelow
    lastColumn := segCols - NEXT_ONE
    if edgeLeft > 0                                                     ' the edge's columns (none when it has no width)
        org
.column
                mov     distance, fromStart                     ' d = head - the column's near edge (> 0 here)
                shl     distance, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                subr    distance, head
                mov     x, distance                             ' G(d / tail)
                shl     x, #SHARE_SHIFT
                qdiv    x, tail
                getqx   x
                call    #.integral
                mov     g0, x
                mov     x, distance                             ' G((d - 1 px) / tail): 0 when d - 1 px <= 0
                sub     x, ##segments.SUBPIXELS
                cmps    x, #NEXT_ONE            wc
    if_c        mov     x, #0                                   ' (the call below changes C, so nothing after it is conditional)
                shl     x, #SHARE_SHIFT
                qdiv    x, tail
                getqx   x
                call    #.integral
                mov     g1, x
                sub     g0, g1                                  ' x tail, / 256: the column's average in Q12
                qmul    g0, tail
                getqx   x
                shr     x, #SUBPIXEL_SHIFT
                mul     x, #LEVEL_FULL                          ' Q12 to 0-255, rounded, at most full
                add     x, ##SHARE_HALF
                shr     x, #SHARE_SHIFT
                fle     x, #LEVEL_FULL
                cmp     bOn, #0                 wz              ' turning off lights the rest
    if_z        subr    x, #LEVEL_FULL
                mov     t1, fromStart                           ' stored from the start end, or mirrored
                cmp     bFromEnd, #0            wz
    if_nz       subr    t1, lastColumn
                add     t1, pLit
                wrbyte  x, t1
                add     fromStart, #NEXT_ONE
                djnz    edgeLeft, #.column
                ret
.integral                                                       ' x (Q12, >= 0) -> G(x), Q12
                cmp     x, ##SHARE_ONE          wc
    if_c        mul     x, x
    if_c        shr     x, #SQUARE_HALF_SHIFT
    if_nc       sub     x, ##SHARE_HALF
                ret

x               long    0
g0              long    0
g1              long    0
t1              long    0
        end

PRI turnOnDigit(digit) | toSegments, bitIndex
' Show a digit from blank: each of its segments grows in (spec R-5.6), horizontals left to right, verticals
' top down, through the normal motion.

    toSegments := byte[@segmentsByDigit][digit]
    repeat bitIndex from LAST_SEGMENT to 0
        if toSegments & (NEXT_ONE << bitIndex)
            if slotVertical[bitIndex]
                segments[bitIndex].commandSegment(segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN)
            else
                segments[bitIndex].commandSegment(segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT)
    bNeedsRender := TRUE

PRI reconfigureForDigit(digitValue) | pLtTable, pRtTable, actionIndex, segmentIndex, nextAction
' Start the transition from the value shown to digitValue: the generated table's commands, or a first showing.

    if currValue <> digitValue
        if digitValue == DIGIT_HIDDEN
            morphOut()
        elseif currValue < 0
            turnOnDigit(digitValue)
        else
            pLtTable := @@leftPtrs[currValue]
            pRtTable := @@LONG[pLtTable][digitValue]
            if pRtTable <> NO_ACTIONS
                actionIndex := 0
                repeat
                    nextAction := BYTE[pRtTable][actionIndex++]
                    if nextAction <> 0
                        segmentIndex := (nextAction & segments.MASK_SEGMENT) >> segments.SEGMENT_ID_SHIFT - NEXT_ONE
                        segments[segmentIndex].commandSegment(nextAction)
                    else
                        quit
            bNeedsRender := TRUE
    currValue := digitValue

CON ' table markers

  NO_ACTIONS = 0

DAT ' digit shapes and the generated transition table

segmentsByDigit
    byte    %0111_1110   ' 0 abcdef-
    byte    %0011_0000   ' 1 -bc----
    byte    %0110_1101   ' 2 ab-de-g
    byte    %0111_1001   ' 3 abcd--g
    byte    %0011_0011   ' 4 -bc--fg
    byte    %0101_1011   ' 5 a-cd-fg
    byte    %0101_1111   ' 6 a-cdefg
    byte    %0111_0000   ' 7 abc----
    byte    %0111_1111   ' 8 abcdefg
    byte    %0111_1011   ' 9 abcd-fg

' NEW TABLE of Actions:
'leftPtrsActual  long    0
'leftPtrsAddr    long    @leftPtrs
'objectOffset    long    0

' NOTE from spin2 doc pg4 symbol standing alone inherits last declared type!!
' =======================================================================================================================
leftPtrs LONG @tableLt0, @tableLt1, @tableLt2, @tableLt3, @tableLt4, @tableLt5, @tableLt6, @tableLt7, @tableLt8, @tableLt9
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tableLt0
    LONG NO_ACTIONS, @fm0_1, @fm0_2, @fm0_3, @fm0_4, @fm0_5, @fm0_6, @fm0_7, @fm0_8, @fm0_9
tableLt1
    LONG @fm1_0, NO_ACTIONS, @fm1_2, @fm1_3, @fm1_4, @fm1_5, @fm1_6, @fm1_7, @fm1_8, @fm1_9
tableLt2
    LONG @fm2_0, @fm2_1, NO_ACTIONS, @fm2_3, @fm2_4, @fm2_5, @fm2_6, @fm2_7, @fm2_8, @fm2_9
tableLt3
    LONG @fm3_0, @fm3_1, @fm3_2, NO_ACTIONS, @fm3_4, @fm3_5, @fm3_6, @fm3_7, @fm3_8, @fm3_9
tableLt4
    LONG @fm4_0, @fm4_1, @fm4_2, @fm4_3, NO_ACTIONS, @fm4_5, @fm4_6, @fm4_7, @fm4_8, @fm4_9
tableLt5
    LONG @fm5_0, @fm5_1, @fm5_2, @fm5_3, @fm5_4, NO_ACTIONS, @fm5_6, @fm5_7, @fm5_8, @fm5_9
tableLt6
    LONG @fm6_0, @fm6_1, @fm6_2, @fm6_3, @fm6_4, @fm6_5, NO_ACTIONS, @fm6_7, @fm6_8, @fm6_9
tableLt7
    LONG @fm7_0, @fm7_1, @fm7_2, @fm7_3, @fm7_4, @fm7_5, @fm7_6, NO_ACTIONS, @fm7_8, @fm7_9
tableLt8
    LONG @fm8_0, @fm8_1, @fm8_2, @fm8_3, @fm8_4, @fm8_5, @fm8_6, @fm8_7, NO_ACTIONS, @fm8_9
tableLt9
    LONG @fm9_0, @fm9_1, @fm9_2, @fm9_3, @fm9_4, @fm9_5, @fm9_6, @fm9_7, @fm9_8, NO_ACTIONS
' =======================================================================================================================


fm0_1
	' transition #1: digit 0 -> 1
	' 4 segments changing, #ON=0, #OFF=4
	' seg[a] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes OFF towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[d] turning OFF while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes OFF towards [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [c] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [e] slides RIGHT to [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_COL_TO_RT
	' seg[f] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [f] slides RIGHT to [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_COL_TO_RT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_2
	' transition #2: digit 0 -> 2
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=2
	' seg[c] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [c] snakes OFF towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_C + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[f] turning OFF while [a] is staying ON.
	' Segment [f] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_3
	' transition #3: digit 0 -> 3
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=2
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [d] is staying ON.
	' Segment [e] snakes OFF towards [d]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	' seg[f] turning OFF while [a] is staying ON.
	' Segment [f] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_4
	' transition #4: digit 0 -> 4
	' 4 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=3
	' seg[a] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes OFF towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[d] turning OFF while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes OFF towards [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [g] is turning ON.
	' Segment [e] snakes OFF towards [g]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_5
	' transition #5: digit 0 -> 5
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=2
	' seg[b] turning OFF while [a] is staying ON.
	' Segment [b] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_B + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [d] is staying ON.
	' Segment [e] snakes OFF towards [d]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_6
	' transition #6: digit 0 -> 6
	' 2 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=1
	' seg[b] turning OFF while [a] is staying ON.
	' Segment [b] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_B + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_7
	' transition #7: digit 0 -> 7
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=0, #OFF=3
	' seg[d] turning OFF while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes OFF towards [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [c] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [e] slides RIGHT to [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_COL_TO_RT
	' seg[f] turning OFF while [a] is staying ON.
	' Segment [f] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_8
	' transition #8: digit 0 -> 8
	' 1 segment changing, #ON=1, #OFF=0
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm0_9
	' transition #9: digit 0 -> 9
	' 2 segments changing, #ON=1, #OFF=1
	' seg[e] turning OFF while [d] is staying ON.
	' Segment [e] snakes OFF towards [d]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_0
	' transition #10: digit 1 -> 0
	' 4 segments changing, #ON=4, #OFF=0
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[e] turning ON while [g] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [e] snakes ON towards [g]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[f] turning ON while [g] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [f] snakes ON towards [g]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_2
	' transition #11: digit 1 -> 2
	' 5 segments changing, #ON=4, #OFF=1
	' seg[c] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [c] snakes OFF towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_C + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON towards [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[e] turning ON while [f] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [e] snakes ON towards [f]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_3
	' transition #12: digit 1 -> 3
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=3, #OFF=0
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_4
	' transition #13: digit 1 -> 4
	' 2 segments changing, #ON=2, #OFF=0
	' seg[f] turning ON while [a] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [f] snakes ON towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_5
	' transition #14: digit 1 -> 5
	' 5 segments changing, #ON=4, #OFF=1
	' seg[b] turning OFF while [a] is turning ON.
	' Segment [b] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_B + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[f] turning ON while [e] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [f] snakes ON towards [e]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_6
	' transition #15: digit 1 -> 6
	' 6 segments changing, #ON=5, #OFF=1
	' seg[b] turning OFF while [a] is turning ON.
	' Segment [b] snakes OFF towards [a]
	byte	segments.SEG_RIGHT_B + segments.CMD_TURN_OFF + segments.CMD_BOTTOM_UP
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[e] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [e] slides LEFT from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_COL_TO_LT
	' seg[f] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' VERT Segment [f] slides LEFT from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_COL_TO_LT
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is turning OFF.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON towards [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_LT_TO_RT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_7
	' transition #16: digit 1 -> 7
	' 1 segment changing, #ON=1, #OFF=0
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_8
	' transition #17: digit 1 -> 8
	' 5 segments changing, #ON=5, #OFF=0
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[e] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [e] slides LEFT from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_E + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_COL_TO_LT
	' seg[f] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' VERT Segment [f] slides LEFT from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_COL_TO_LT
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm1_9
	' transition #18: digit 1 -> 9
	' 4 segments changing, #ON=4, #OFF=0
	' seg[a] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [a] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_TOP_A + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[d] turning ON while [c] is staying ON.
	' Segment [d] snakes ON away from [c]
	byte	segments.SEG_BOTTOM_D + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	' seg[f] turning ON while [e] is staying OFF.
	' Segment [f] snakes ON towards [e]
	byte	segments.SEG_LEFT_F + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_TOP_DOWN
	' seg[g] turning ON while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes ON away from [b]
	byte	segments.SEG_MIDDLE_G + segments.CMD_TURN_ON + segments.CMD_RT_TO_LT
	byte	0	' terminate entry

fm2_0
	' transition #19: digit 2 -> 0
	' 3 segments changing, #ON=2, #OFF=1
	' seg[g] turning OFF while [b] is staying ON.
	' Segment [g] snakes OFF towards [b]
